# Copy tone (Adamas Materials)

Write like a materials supplier, not a SaaS landing page.

## Do not use
- Rhetorical CTA questions: "Ready to discuss…?", "Need a technical answer?", "Let's talk"
- Fake-precision slogans: "CONNECT WITH PRECISION", "Material Solutions.", "Unlock", "Empower", "Leverage", "Transform", "Journey", "World-class", "Cutting-edge", "Seamless"
- Deployed-teams fluff: "specialized teams are deployed", "end-to-end", "full-scale industrial production" as filler
- Invented metrics or badges (e.g. "99.99%", "ISO 2026") unless the user supplies real figures
- Attribution quote blocks that sound like brand slogans

## Prefer
- Short factual statements: what the material is for, what to send in an RFQ
- Direct labels: Contact, RFQ, Markets, Specs
- Concrete markets already on the site: cutting tools, data-center cooling, semiconductors, universities, technical solutions
- CVD-only scope; no HPHT or jewelry unless asked
